<title>UK: UK June non-EU trade deficit 713 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK June non-EU trade deficit 713 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released following seasonally adjusted UK non-EU Trade data in June -</p>
<p>    UK TRADE NON-EU (in million stg)   June     May   (Prel May)</p>
<p>    Trade balance			   -713     -584	(-563)</p>
<p>    Exports (FOB)			  6,278    6,370   (6,397)</p>
<p>    Imports (FOB)			  6,991    6,954   (6,960)</p>
<p>    Oil exports				177	223     (223)</p>
<p>    Oil imports				342	324     (324)</p>
<p>    Trade balance 3m ending June    -1,715	N/A  (-1,639)</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecast 597 million stg deficit.  </p>
<p>TRADE VOLUME EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Import volume index (base 1990) 153.3    153.1   (153.8)</p>
<p>    Export volume index (base 1990) 148.6    146.5   (146.9)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)  +7.0%   +3.0%    (3.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (imps)  +9.5%   +6.5%    (7.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)  +5.0%   +4.0%    (4.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (exps) +11.0%   +9.0%    (9.5%)</p>
<p>TRADE VALUE EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Balance (million stg)		-224    -305     (-310)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)  +6.5%   +2.0%    (2.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)  +7.0%   +3.5%    (3.5%)</p>
<p>The ONS said provisional estimates show both export and import prices little changed compared with May.</p>
</text>
